-This task uses computer vision to determine the health of a coral colony by comparing a current image to an image taken one year ago
-This task uses computer vision to determine the health of a coral colony by comparing a current image to an image taken one year ago


-Load the baseline coral image (1 year ago) and its masks
-Align the new coral image to the old image
-Convert the new image to HSV color space for stable color detection
- Detect:
	•	Pink coral using HSV thresholds
	•	White (bleached) coral using HSV thresholds
 changes:
	•	Bleaching = old pink => new white
	•	Recovery = old white => new pink
-Draw bounding rectangles around detected regions and save results
